- content_for :og_image, asset_url('kluster-single.png')

= render 'shared/breakthrough_page', page_title: 'The Kluster', current_page: 'The Kluster', page_subtitle: "To quote a friend, 'This is way too much effort for Christmas Lights'", document_title: 'The Kluster - About Baldrick', meta: ['In-house test lab', 'Every board variant', 'Remote monitoring'] do
  p.lead The Kluster is our state-of-the-art development and testing system where we design, prototype, and validate all Baldrick products before they reach our customers. But it didn't start that way — it began with a customer's problem and some old plywood.

  .prose
    figure.figure
      .fimg
        = image_tag 'kluster-inprocess.jpeg', alt: 'The Kluster development system showing multiple Baldrick boards mounted on wooden framework'
      figcaption The Kluster in progress — multiple Baldrick boards mounted on a wooden test framework.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Origin story
      | How The Kluster came about

    p
      | The story begins with one of our customers who was having issues with 15
      = link_to ' Baldrick8 boards', board_path('baldrick8')
      |  on a large mega tree. When Dom heard about the problem, he knew he needed a way to replicate and test the setup to understand what was going wrong.
    p So Dom took some old plywood he had received, cut up a load of positive and negative cables, found 24 Baldrick boards and added a pixel to each. This simple setup became the foundation of what we now call The Kluster.

    figure.figure
      .fimg
        = image_tag 'kluster-old.png', alt: 'Early version of The Kluster with Baldrick boards mounted on plywood with basic wiring'
      figcaption The early days — Baldrick boards mounted on plywood with basic power distribution.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Evolution
      | From simple testing to smart monitoring

    p After fixing some pixel issues, we expanded The Kluster to have a monitoring system called Edmund which monitors all development data from the boards and allows us to test new features for issues.
    p Being a remote team, we wanted the ability to press buttons and turn off boards without someone physically present, so The Kluster and Edmund were expanded to manage relays and have an API for end-to-end testing.
    p Today, Edmund and The Kluster do pixel colour monitoring, allowing us to track and analyse the performance of individual pixels across all our test boards in real time.

    figure.figure
      .fimg
        = image_tag 'kluster-two.png', alt: 'Current Kluster setup showing multiple KLUSTER boards with glowing green LEDs in a grid arrangement'
      figcaption The current Kluster setup with multiple boards and monitoring systems.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Today
      | The Kluster now

    p The Kluster now has instances of every board and revision in the Baldrick family (and a few not yet released) and is still under continuous development. We've recently upgraded Dom's old plywood for some good-looking laser cut mounts and we've got some custom PCBs on the way to help us monitor a bit more.

    figure.figure
      .fimg
        = image_tag 'kluster-single.png', alt: 'Single KLUSTER board showing detailed components and connections'
      figcaption A single Kluster board showing the detailed components and monitoring capabilities.

    .callout.info
      span.ic
        svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
          path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"
          circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
      div
        span.lbl Continuous innovation
        p.bd The Kluster is constantly evolving, from simple plywood mounts to sophisticated monitoring systems.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Edmund
      | Our smart monitoring system

    p Edmund is the brain behind The Kluster — our custom monitoring system that tracks everything from power consumption to pixel performance. It allows our remote team to:

    .spec-grid
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M12 2v4M5 7l3 3M19 7l-3 3M5 17l3-3M19 17l-3-3M12 18v4"
        h4 Remote control
        p Power boards on/off remotely, monitor real-time performance and test new firmware features from anywhere.
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M4 19h16M4 15h16M4 11h16M4 7h16"
        h4 Data collection
        p Track power consumption, monitor temperature, log error conditions and generate test reports.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Validation
      | What we test

    p The Kluster houses every Baldrick board variant, allowing us to test new features across our entire product line before release. This ensures that when you buy a Baldrick product, it's been thoroughly tested in real-world conditions.

    ul
      li
        strong Hardware testing
        |  — every board revision is tested for power efficiency, thermal performance and reliability under various load conditions.
      li
        strong Firmware validation
        |  — new firmware features are tested across all board variants to ensure compatibility and performance.
      li
        strong Real-world simulation
        |  — we simulate actual customer setups to catch issues before they reach our customers.
      li
        strong Long-term reliability
        |  — boards run continuously to ensure they can handle the demands of seasonal lighting displays.

    .callout.warn
      span.ic
        svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
          path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"
          path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"
      div
        span.lbl Always evolving
        p.bd From plywood to laser-cut mounts, The Kluster continues to grow and improve with every iteration.

    h3 The Kluster legacy
    p What started as a simple solution to a customer's problem has grown into our most valuable development tool. The Kluster represents our commitment to quality and our willingness to solve problems with whatever materials we have at hand.
    p Every Baldrick product you use has been tested in The Kluster, ensuring it meets our high standards for reliability and performance.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Keep reading
      | Related breakthroughs

    .next-grid
